---
import AboutPage from '../../../components/AboutPage.astro';
import Bi from '../../../components/Bi.astro';
import { langPaths, type Lang } from '../../../i18n/index.ts';
import { REPO_URL } from '../../../i18n/common.ts';
import { langPath } from '../../../lib/url.ts';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';

export const getStaticPaths = langPaths;
const lang = Astro.params.lang as Lang;
const BY_SA = 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode';
const BY_SA_DEED = lang === 'it' ? 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.it' : 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en';
// Notices of the code the 3D viewer downloads (3Dmol.js and what its build bundles), read from the installed packages (D050).
const pkg = (p: string) => readFileSync(`${process.cwd()}/node_modules/${p}`, 'utf8').trim();
// The zlib notice is the comment block at the top of pako's zlib port.
const zlibNotice = (pkg('pako/lib/zlib/inflate.js').match(/^'use strict';\s*\n((?:\/\/.*\n)+)/)?.[1] ?? '')
  .replace(/^\/\/ ?/gm, '')
  .trim();
if (!zlibNotice.includes('Jean-loup Gailly')) throw new Error('licenses.astro: zlib notice not found in pako');
const notices = [
  { name: '3Dmol.js 2.5.5', license: 'BSD-3-Clause', text: pkg('3dmol/LICENSE') },
  { name: 'pako 2.2.0 / 1.0.11', license: 'MIT AND Zlib', text: `${pkg('pako/LICENSE')}\n\n${zlibNotice}` },
  { name: 'iobuffer 5.4.0', license: 'MIT', text: pkg('iobuffer/LICENSE') },
  { name: 'netcdfjs 3.0.0', license: 'MIT', text: pkg('netcdfjs/LICENSE') },
  { name: 'upng-js 2.1.0', license: 'MIT', text: pkg('upng-js/LICENSE') },
];
---

<AboutPage lang={lang} slug="licenses">
  <Bi lang={lang}>
    <Fragment slot="it">
      <h2>Codice: MIT</h2>
      <p>
        Il codice del sito è distribuito con <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">licenza MIT</a>:
        puoi usarlo, modificarlo e ridistribuirlo, anche per scopi commerciali, mantenendo l’avviso di copyright.
      </p>
      <h2>Contenuti: CC BY-SA 4.0</h2>
      <p>
        I testi, le domande e gli schemi originali dell’atlante sono distribuiti con licenza{' '}
        <a href={BY_SA_DEED} rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribuzione – Condividi allo stesso modo 4.0</a>{' '}
        (<a href={BY_SA} rel="noopener">testo legale</a>). Puoi copiarli e adattarli se:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>citi “Atlante di Patologia” con un link al sito e indichi se hai fatto modifiche;</li>
        <li>distribuisci i materiali derivati con la stessa licenza.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Immagini di terzi</h2>
      <p>
        Le immagini non create da noi mantengono la propria licenza (pubblico dominio, CC0, CC BY o CC BY-SA), indicata
        sotto ogni immagine e nella pagina <a href={langPath(lang, 'about/credits/')}>Crediti</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Marchi e testi di riferimento</h2>
      <p>
        I titoli dei manuali citati appartengono ai rispettivi editori. Nessun contenuto di quei manuali è riprodotto
        nell’atlante.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="en">
      <h2>Code: MIT</h2>
      <p>
        The site’s code is released under the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">MIT licence</a>: you may
        use, change and redistribute it, commercially too, as long as you keep the copyright notice.
      </p>
      <h2>Content: CC BY-SA 4.0</h2>
      <p>
        The atlas’s original texts, questions and diagrams are released under the{' '}
        <a href={BY_SA_DEED} rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0</a> licence{' '}
        (<a href={BY_SA} rel="noopener">legal code</a>). You may copy and adapt them if you:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>credit “Atlante di Patologia” with a link to the site and say whether you made changes;</li>
        <li>share derived material under the same licence.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Third-party images</h2>
      <p>
        Images we did not create keep their own licence (public domain, CC0, CC BY or CC BY-SA), shown under each image and
        on the <a href={langPath(lang, 'about/credits/')}>Credits</a> page.
      </p>
      <h2>Trademarks and reference texts</h2>
      <p>The titles of the textbooks we cite belong to their publishers. No content from those books is reproduced in the atlas.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Bi>
  <h2 id="third-party-code">{lang === 'it' ? 'Codice di terze parti per la vista 3D' : 'Third-party code in the 3D view'}</h2>
  <Bi lang={lang}>
    <p slot="it">
      La vista 3D dei percorsi molecolari usa 3Dmol.js, scaricato solo quando premi «Carica la vista 3D», insieme alle
      librerie che contiene. Ne riportiamo gli avvisi di copyright e le licenze, come richiedono. I dati strutturali vengono
      dal Protein Data Bank (CC0 1.0) e sono elencati nella pagina <a href={langPath(lang, 'about/credits/')}>Crediti</a>.
    </p>
    <p slot="en">
      The 3D view of the molecular pathways uses 3Dmol.js, downloaded only when you press “Load the 3D view”, together with
      the libraries it bundles. Their copyright notices and licences are reproduced here, as they require. The structure data
      come from the Protein Data Bank (CC0 1.0) and are listed on the <a href={langPath(lang, 'about/credits/')}>Credits</a> page.
    </p>
  </Bi>
  {
    notices.map((n) => (
      <details class="license-notice">
        <summary>
          {n.name} — {n.license}
        </summary>
        <pre lang="en">{n.text}</pre>
      </details>
    ))
  }
</AboutPage>

<style>
  .license-notice pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
